# Phase 4: Repository Analysis API — Walkthrough

## Endpoints Added

| Method | Route | Description |
|--------|-------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/api/projects/:projectId/analyze` | Runs the deterministic analysis engine and persists detected components |
| `GET`  | `/api/projects/:projectId/analysis` | Returns the project's latest detected components |

Both endpoints require authentication via the existing demo JWT cookie.

---

## Service Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Route as POST /analyze Route
    participant Auth as require-auth
    participant AnalysisSvc as analysis.service
    participant Prisma
    participant GitHubSvc as github.service
    participant Detector as detection.service

    Client->>Route: POST /projects/:id/analyze
    Route->>Auth: getAuthUser()
    Auth-->>Route: user | null
    Route->>AnalysisSvc: analyzeProject(projectId, userId)
    AnalysisSvc->>Prisma: project.findUnique (ownership check)
    AnalysisSvc->>Prisma: gitHubConnection.findFirst (get token)
    AnalysisSvc->>GitHubSvc: getRepositoryTree(repo, branch, token)
    GitHubSvc-->>AnalysisSvc: tree
    AnalysisSvc->>Detector: detectComponents(tree, fetchContent)
    Detector->>GitHubSvc: getFileContent (for each config file)
    Detector-->>AnalysisSvc: DetectedComponent[]
    AnalysisSvc->>Prisma: $transaction(deleteMany + createMany)
    AnalysisSvc-->>Route: AnalysisResult
    Route-->>Client: 200 JSON
```

